## findings

### (a) Gate-as-static-subset architecture — PASS
- Membership-only judgment: `crates/sley-vm/src/bootstrap.rs:60-63` is a flat sorted tag table (42 entries, `161` deliberately absent); `bootstrap.rs:406-416` routes `AdapterInvoke` to `admit_bridge_use` and everything else to `binary_search`. No semantics recomputed.
- Single-authority rule is declared and honored: `bootstrap.rs:29-34` names what stays with S20-210/S20-220/lowering/execution; refusals reuse `LowerErrorCode` (`bootstrap.rs:99-101`), so no new refusal vocabulary is minted.
- No execution-path change: `bootstrap.rs:36-40`. Verified structurally — `judge_bootstrap_profile` is referenced only at its definition and from `bootstrap_closure.rs:34,2307,2322,2388` (the closure test/emitter lane). Zero call sites in lowering or execution.
- Full-coverage rule: `bootstrap.rs:224-226` refuses when `reached.len() != functions.len()`. Pre-order rule: `bootstrap.rs:279-280` pushes before descending into callees.
- Cycle refusal is correct as written: `visited` is inserted post-order only (`bootstrap.rs:322-323`), so it can never contain a stack member. Self- and mutual-recursion pinned (`bootstrap.rs:786`, `bootstrap.rs:1019`).

### (b) One-resolution-authority — PASS
`resolve_bridge_entry` is `pub(crate)` at `crates/sley-vm/src/extended.rs:272` with exactly four consumers, matching the claim: surcharge `extended.rs:351` (`bridge_fuel_surcharge`), lowering judgment `extended.rs:1173` (`judge_extended_operation`), execution `extended.rs:1947` (`execute_extended_instruction`), gate `bootstrap.rs:344`. Frozen-field equality (adapter identity, `abi_version == 1`, `Index` failure type, empty effects) is enforced inside the resolver at `extended.rs:291-297`, so purity/registry drift cannot be routed around by any consumer. The registry is a closed three-way branch (`extended.rs:277-285`) — no extensibility surface.

